{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Please send by the hand of him whom You will send.</b> Some say that Moses prophesied that he would not ultimately bring them into the land; therefore 'please send' — now, for 'נָא' denotes immediacy, 'by the hand of him whom You will send' — in the future. And some say that Moses said: even if I begin to go on the mission, I know that I do not have the strength to complete all the matters, for 'כְּבַד פֶּה אָנֹכִי' (Exodus 4:10), and in the end You will send another in my place; therefore please send now by the hand of him whom You will send afterward. And the correct interpretation is that he said this concerning Aaron his older brother, for in the end he had a share in the entire mission; therefore he said: hand over the entire mission into his hand, lest it be evil in his eyes on account of Moses. And the Holy One, blessed be He, answered him: 'וְרָאֲךָ וְשָׂמַח בְּלִבּוֹ' (Exodus 4:14), and it is easy to understand."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:18:19.633166336Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}